public static int squarePermutations(int[] A) {
    int n = A.length;
    int[] dp = new int[n + 1];
    dp[0] = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (int j = 1; j * j <= A[i - 1]; j++) {
            dp[i] += dp[i - j];
        }
    }
    return dp[n];
}
```
This function calculates and returns the number of square permutations of the given array `A`. The algorithm works by using a bottom-up dynamic programming approach, where `dp[i]` represents the number of square permutations of the first `i` elements of `A`.

The base case is `dp[0]`, which is set to 1, as there is only one square permutation of the empty array.

For each `i` from 1 to `n`, we iterate through all possible ways of breaking this array into two parts of sizes `j` and `i - j`. We check if `j * j` is less than or equal to `A[i - 1]`, and if so, we update `dp[i]` by adding `dp[i - j]` to it, as this represents the number of square permutations of the first `i` elements of `A`.

Finally, we return `dp[n]`, which is the total number of square permutations of `A`.

This approach has a time complexity of O(n * n) and a space complexity of O(n), where `n` is the length of the input array `A`.

```
public static int squarePermutations(int[] A) {
    int n = A.length;
    int[] permutations = new int[n];
    int count = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        permutations[i] = i;
    }

    while (true) {
        int[] temp = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            temp[i] = A[permutations[i]];
        }

        boolean isSquare = true;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            int sum = temp[i] + temp[i + 1];
            if (!(Math.sqrt(sum) == (int) Math.sqrt(sum))) {
                isSquare = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (isSquare) {
            count++;
        }

        int i = n - 1;
        while (i > 0 && permutations[i - 1] > permutations[i]) {
            i--;
        }
        if (i <= 0) {
            break;
        }
        int j = n - 1;
        while (permutations[j] <= permutations[i - 1]) {
            j--;
        }
        swap(permutations, i - 1, j);
        for (int k = i; k < n; k++) {
            int maxVal = n - 1;
            for (int l = k; l < n; l++) {
                if (permutations[l] < permutations[k - 1]) {
                    maxVal = permutations[l];
                    break;
                }
            }
            permutations[k] = maxVal;
        }
    }

    return count;
}

public static void swap(int[] A, int i, int j) {
    int temp = A[i];
    A[i] = A[j];
    A[j] = temp;
}
